  "ingredients": [
    "1 (14 pound) roast-ready prime rib roast (ribs cut off and tied to roast)",
    "aluminum foil",
    "0.75 cup all-purpose flour",
    "2 teaspoons freshly ground black pepper",
    "2 teaspoons salt",
    "2 teaspoons paprika",
    "1 teaspoon onion powder",
    "0.5 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "0.25 teaspoon celery seed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Remove rib roast from the refrigerator. Allow it to come to room temperature for about 3 hours, depending on its size.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/FNphy06pWiGQM4KbViEtjnA8Nbc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/139890-restaurant-style-prime-rib-roast-VAT-step-01-425dea5935d04447bb05273a305ecef5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/139890/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 425 degrees F (220 degrees C). Line a roasting pan with aluminum foil.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/a19WBFadiYJPK9ZQqtYEPLd59g8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/139890-restaurant-style-prime-rib-roast-VAT-step-02-58d3d7057c0447a2ab24950196bdcc50.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/139890/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place rib roast onto the prepared roasting pan; blot with paper towels. Sift together flour, pepper, salt, paprika, onion powder, garlic powder, and celery seed into a bowl. Coat roast all over with flour mixture.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/qTXdaMvs-u3GitHzFwb6Q0sChc8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/139890-restaurant-style-prime-rib-roast-VAT-step-03-5c7bffca10a34956ab560dd0624d5d17.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/139890/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast in the preheated oven until cooked to your desired degree of doneness, about 4 1/2 hours (20 minutes a pound) for medium-rare. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read at least 120 degrees F (49 degrees C) for medium-rare, 130 degrees F (54 degrees C) for medium, or 140 degrees F (60 degrees C) for well-done.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/UHcpDJDjVhHJE7fHyaotS7Xka1M=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/139890-restaurant-style-prime-rib-roast-VAT-step-04-24038d262f77400c968287e7c2b751b5.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/139890/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cover roast with aluminum foil. Let rest on the counter in a warm spot for 30 minutes to 1 hour before slicing.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/YUC_Ee8PwWhJOWqjMD-pDrwAjgM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/139890-restaurant-style-prime-rib-roast-VAT-step-05-f07a8d2307024173bb77315138901cb4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/139890/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/JkE9Oq3wjPNhFli6URzB3jv4KtA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/139890-restaurant-style-prime-rib-roast-VAT-Beauty-4x3-49e22d94f3444ebaad7995f263643031.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/139890/step_06.webp"
    }
